# Hardcode Detection Protocol (Zero Tolerance)

## Rule
When reviewing or writing code, if you detect ANY hardcoded URL, institution name, CSS selector, or magic value outside the centralized config — **STOP the current task immediately**.

## Action
Report to the user:
> "HARDCODE TESPİTİ: `[file:line]` — `[the hardcoded value]`. Bunu SaaS yapısına uygun olarak Config'e taşıyalım mı?"

## What Counts as Hardcoded
- Domain URLs outside `core/config.py` (e.g., `"https://obs.ozal.edu.tr"` in a scraper file)
- CSS selectors outside `SELECTORS` dict in `core/config.py`
- Error messages containing institution-specific names
- Endpoint paths not defined in config constants
- Any university-specific data (name, logo path, theme color) outside the tenant config system

## Exceptions (ONLY these are acceptable)
- Centralized constants in `core/config.py` — this IS the config layer for Phase 1 (scraper). These values are CRITICAL and must never be lost during refactoring.
- HTTP headers and standard protocol values (User-Agent, Accept, etc.)
- Test fixtures and mock data
- Python standard library constants
- Logging format strings (not user-facing)

## Config Data Preservation (CRITICAL)
`core/config.py` contains irreplaceable scraper URLs, CSS selectors, and form field identifiers. During any refactor or migration:
1. Audit every value in `config.py` before modifying
2. Ensure ALL values are preserved in the new location
3. NEVER delete a config value without confirming it's migrated
